Performance: Generated TypeScript unions keep the first case of each runtime test (`typeof`, `Array.isArray`, `instanceof`) as its plain value, with no wrapper object; only cases sharing that test, or without one, keep `{ case, value }`. Regenerate, and narrow a direct case by its test and a tagged one by `case`. On sampled GitHub runners, tagged-union writes took 14–16 % less time on x64 and 20 % less on Neoverse-N2, and tagged reads about 12 % less on AMD EPYC and 17 % less on Neoverse-N2.
